starting to age, with classrooms and science labs that have seen little to no modernization and were built for a
different era of education.
• This past year, the District recorded over 138 roof leaks, and the aging air-conditioning systems are increasingly
unable to keep up during extreme heat.
• Currently, students attend classes in more than 81 portable classrooms that are over 20 years old. Many of these
classrooms suffer from water leaks, structural damage and other ongoing maintenance challenges.
