IMPARTIAL ANALYSIS OF MEASURE D
This Impartial Analysis of Measure D has been prepared by the City Attorney pursuant to Section 9280 of
the California Elections Code.
The City Council of the City of Needles has placed Measure D on the ballot for the November 3, 2026 General Municipal
Election. Measure D would amend Section 503 of the City Charter to increase the compensation paid to each member of
the City Council from one dollar ($1.00) per month to one hundred fifty dollars ($150.00) per month.
Effect of Measure on Existing Law:
The City of Needles is a charter city operating under a City Charter adopted by the voters in 1958. Section 503 of the
Charter currently provides that each member of the City Council shall receive compensation in the amount of one dollar
($1.00) per month. That amount has remained unchanged since the Charter was adopted approximately sixty-eight years
ago.
Because the amount of City Council compensation is established by the City Charter, it may not be changed by ordinance
or resolution of the City Council. Under the California Constitution and applicable law governing charter cities, any
amendment to the Charter, including a change to City Council compensation, must be approved by the voters.
If approved, Measure D would amend Section 503 of the City Charter to establish compensation for each City Council
Member at one hundred fifty dollars ($150.00) per month. The measure would not modify any other provision of Section
503. Existing Charter provisions authorizing reimbursement for actual and necessary travel and other official expenses
incurred in the performance of official duties would remain unchanged. The measure would not authorize any additional
salary, benefits, or compensation beyond that expressly provided in the Charter.
If approved, the City has determined Measure D would result in an additional annual cost of $20,916 to the City. Pursuant
to State law, approval of Measure D requires a majority vote of the City's voters who vote in the election.
If approved, the amendment would become effective following certification of the election results and completion of all
procedures required by law for charter amendments.
A "Yes" vote is a vote in favor of amending Section 503 of the City Charter to increase City Council compensation from
one dollar ($1.00) per month to one hundred fifty dollars ($150.00) per month.
A "No" vote is a vote against the proposed Charter amendment, and Section 503 of the City Charter would remain
unchanged, with City Council compensation continuing at one dollar ($1.00) per month.
The above statement is an impartial analysis of Measure D. If you desire a copy of the Measure, please call the
City Clerk's office at (760) 326-2113 and a copy will be mailed at no cost to you, or you may obtain a copy by
visiting the City's website at www.cityofneedles.com
