ARGUMENT IN FAVOR OF MEASURE R
This Argument in Favor of Measure R was submitted pursuant to Section 9315 of the California Elections
Code. It is the opinion of the author(s), and has been printed exactly as submitted.
Since 1985, Rim of the World Recreation and Park District, governed by a locally elected Board, consistently has served a
110-square-mile area by operating twelve parks, a sports complex, community spaces, two community centers and a
range of programs for residents.
The District receives no state or county funding for ongoing operations and relies on the current $22-per-year Special
Parcel Tax paid by property owners within its boundaries. The Special Parcel Tax currently provides approximately 70%
of the District's $1.1 million annual operating budget.
As costs continue to rise, the District has taken significant steps to reduce expenditures, reducing staffing and overhead,
conducting a comprehensive fee study to align program fees with actual costs, and designating a number of cost cutting
measures. The District has also remained debt-free, demonstrating a strong commitment to fiscal responsibility. Despite
these efforts, revenues cannot keep pace with increasing insurance, utility, maintenance, and repair costs, putting at risk
the District's ability to continue to provide consistent recreational facilities and programs for the community.
