programs to prepare students for good-paying careers in nursing, teaching and firefighting; removing asbestos and mold;
repairing deteriorating gas lines; upgrading emergency communications systems; upgrading campus safety and security,
including fire safety systems; providing safe drinking water; repairing and upgrading classrooms and labs; repairing and
upgrading air conditioning and heating systems; earthquake retrofitting school buildings and classrooms; creating a
community college center in the mountain area of the District; upgrading classrooms and labs and career training facilities
for nursing, teaching, and firefighting; improving student centers to provide job training, job placement, counseling, and
support services to students; and other repair, renovation and construction projects.
